From: x86QW maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] use pointer width for interpreted QVM syscall arguments

MVDSV's idx64 macro describes the x86-64 JIT target, not every host with
64-bit pointers. VM_CallInterpreted2 nevertheless uses it to decide
whether the QVM's 32-bit syscall arguments need widening to intptr_t.
On Apple Silicon adjacent arguments are combined into invalid pointers
during GAME_INIT. Test the actual pointer width without enabling x86 JIT
code on arm64.

--- a/src/vm_interpreted.c
+++ b/src/vm_interpreted.c
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@ int VM_CallInterpreted2(vm_t *vm, int nargs, int *args)
 				//vm->programStack = programStack - 4;
 				vm->programStack = programStack - 8;
 				*(int *)&image[ programStack + 4 ] = ~r0.i;
-#if idx64 //__WORDSIZE == 64
+#if INTPTR_MAX == INT64_MAX
 					// the vm has ints on the stack, we expect
 					// longs so we have to convert it
